{"card_hash": "0452ee1ac715f57319b6a4ad08a7956ef380e6e2674285a832930b4a6ea1776e", "channel": "AI Engineer", "chars": 17907, "chars_all_clips": 17907, "chars_chosen_clips": 1440, "clip_count": 15, "clips": [{"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=v3Fr2JR47KA\u0026t=16s", "end": 94.75, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "c765f83a3809ee167e3fd4c21a7e0b54e82d8e7a3e0251fabdd66eb7aaf656f6", "start": 16.75, "text": "\u003e\u003e Well, welcome. Let's get started. This is an MCP application. That's an agent shipping its own interface not through like a plugin, not through an SDK, not rendered on the fly by the model on the client side, or hardcoded into the produc", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=v3Fr2JR47KA\u0026t=200s", "end": 359.07, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "57cab1c2f7f5d6167f66059f7339d9bc730790ef2869352d7bfddb91449b15c0", "start": 200.12, "text": " capabilities of the model increasing, we're going into a new era, which I think this year will be we will see the start, where we're not just doing coding agents, we're going to have general agents that will do real knowledge worker stuff,", "timing": "coarse", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=v3Fr2JR47KA\u0026t=359s", "end": 432.11, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "fb18efcf8c417fa075b419fe835171b4c8be0c47f124f20f5466fb9f3a26d3b9", "start": 359.08, "text": "platform. Of course, CLIs very popular when local coding agents. It's an amazing tool to get simply started, to have something that you can pose in a bash, that you that automatically discover where the model can automatically discover what", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=v3Fr2JR47KA\u0026t=485s", "end": 602.15, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "798d9f69413c72c900a372129605c1535535852c617a2792a5a3ecb2cfb473c2", "start": 485.67, "text": "And the number one thing we're going to do there, and what we all have to do, and something I want to really get across today, is that we need to go and start building something called progressive discovery. Most people when they think abou", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=v3Fr2JR47KA\u0026t=760s", "end": 844.949, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "ddb656d024c7b6b30b647251fae3ae113e9406d10e0c922602027b93ed6dfd37", "start": 760.32, "text": "agent. If you want to orchestrate things together, you should reach, of course, for programmatic tool calling, and you can do this on the client side, as I said before, but you can also do this on the server side. The Cloudflare MCP server ", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=v3Fr2JR47KA\u0026t=844s", "end": 958.75, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "5417ae42abad0ccb5a7710cebdcc2e17d2c4c9744e8c1472af173c612fb00549", "start": 844.96, "text": "\u003e\u003e [snorts] \u003e\u003e And so, we have a proposal from our friends at Google, who are working on something called a stateless transport protocol, which make it significantly easier to just treat MCP servers like you know, another stateless uh rest ", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}], "current_topic": "AI and ML", "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpts": [{"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=v3Fr2JR47KA\u0026t=16s", "end": 94.75, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "c765f83a3809ee167e3fd4c21a7e0b54e82d8e7a3e0251fabdd66eb7aaf656f6", "start": 16.75, "text": "\u003e\u003e Well, welcome. Let's get started. This is an MCP application. That's an agent shipping its own interface not through like a plugin, not through an SDK, not rendered on the fly by the model on the client side, or hardcoded into the produc", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=v3Fr2JR47KA\u0026t=200s", "end": 359.07, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "57cab1c2f7f5d6167f66059f7339d9bc730790ef2869352d7bfddb91449b15c0", "start": 200.12, "text": " capabilities of the model increasing, we're going into a new era, which I think this year will be we will see the start, where we're not just doing coding agents, we're going to have general agents that will do real knowledge worker stuff,", "timing": "coarse", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=v3Fr2JR47KA\u0026t=359s", "end": 432.11, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "fb18efcf8c417fa075b419fe835171b4c8be0c47f124f20f5466fb9f3a26d3b9", "start": 359.08, "text": "platform. Of course, CLIs very popular when local coding agents. It's an amazing tool to get simply started, to have something that you can pose in a bash, that you that automatically discover where the model can automatically discover what", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=v3Fr2JR47KA\u0026t=485s", "end": 602.15, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "798d9f69413c72c900a372129605c1535535852c617a2792a5a3ecb2cfb473c2", "start": 485.67, "text": "And the number one thing we're going to do there, and what we all have to do, and something I want to really get across today, is that we need to go and start building something called progressive discovery. Most people when they think abou", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=v3Fr2JR47KA\u0026t=760s", "end": 844.949, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "ddb656d024c7b6b30b647251fae3ae113e9406d10e0c922602027b93ed6dfd37", "start": 760.32, "text": "agent. If you want to orchestrate things together, you should reach, of course, for programmatic tool calling, and you can do this on the client side, as I said before, but you can also do this on the server side. The Cloudflare MCP server ", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=v3Fr2JR47KA\u0026t=844s", "end": 958.75, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "5417ae42abad0ccb5a7710cebdcc2e17d2c4c9744e8c1472af173c612fb00549", "start": 844.96, "text": "\u003e\u003e [snorts] \u003e\u003e And so, we have a proposal from our friends at Google, who are working on something called a stateless transport protocol, which make it significantly easier to just treat MCP servers like you know, another stateless uh rest ", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}], "hint": null, "platform": "youtube", "profile": "librarian", "schema_version": 1, "selection_version": "spread-longest-v1", "slug": "The_Future_of_MCP_David_Soria_Parra_Anthropic", "source_revision": "b006c956a2d5df55c8f74e4c159cbc67dfa9c8577e29f51813770dc32a920538", "source_type": "video", "status": "evidenced", "summary_hint": null, "title": "The Future of MCP — David Soria Parra, Anthropic", "topic": "AI and ML", "truncated": true, "truncation": {"byte_budget": true, "fields": ["hint"], "selection": true}, "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=v3Fr2JR47KA", "video_id": "v3Fr2JR47KA", "yoinked_at": "2026-05-17T18:01:32"}
